.TH "easel printseq" 1 "@EASEL_DATE@" "Easel @EASEL_VERSION@" "Easel Manual"

.SH NAME
easel printseq \- print a nucleic acid sequence with complement and/or translation


.SH SYNOPSIS

.B easel printseq
[\fIoptions\fR]
.I seqfile


.SH DESCRIPTION

.PP
Given a
.I seqfile
containing a nucleic acid sequence (DNA or RNA),
.B easel printseq
prints the sequence to
.I stdout
in a human-readable format, with both strands shown by default and with
coordinate numbering at the left and right of each line.

.PP
The format of
.I seqfile
and its alphabet (DNA or RNA) are autodetected, but can be asserted
explicitly with the
.BR \-\-informat ,
.BR \-\-dna ,
and
.B \-\-rna
options. Protein sequence input is rejected.

.PP
The default output is double-stranded, in lines of 60 nucleotides
broken into groups of 10 separated by spaces, with the top strand
numbered at the left (start of line) and right (end of line):

.nf
   1: ATTATTATCC ATTACACGAA GATTTAGTAT CATCTTTTTC TTAACTCTCC ACTTGCAAAG 60
    : TAATAATAGG TAATGTGCTT CTAAATCATA GTAGAAAAAG AATTGAGAGG TGAACGTTTC

  61: TTGCAGCCTT TGCGGTCGCT TCATCAATAT TGCCTACCAA ATAAAAAGCT TGTTCAGGAA 120
    : AACGTCGGAA ACGCCAGCGA AGTAGTTATA ACGGATGGTT TATTTTTCGA ACAAGTCCTT
.fi

.PP
Only the first sequence in
.I seqfile
is formatted and printed.

.PP
With the
.B \-a
option, the three top-strand reading frames are translated and shown
underneath the sequence in single-letter amino acid code. Because the
amino acid letters are spaced to align with their codons, grouping is
turned off (the
.B \-a
option sets and requires
.BR "\-g 0" ).

.nf
      1: ATTATTATCCATTACACGAAGATTTAGTATCATCTTTTTCTTAACTCTCCACTTGCAAAG 60
       : TAATAATAGGTAATGTGCTTCTAAATCATAGTAGAAAAAGAATTGAGAGGTGAACGTTTC
     0 : I  I  I  H  Y  T  K  I  *  Y  H  L  F  L  N  S  P  L  A  K
     1 :  L  L  S  I  T  R  R  F  S  I  I  F  F  L  T  L  H  L  Q  S
     2 :   Y  Y  P  L  H  E  D  L  V  S  S  F  S  *  L  S  T  C  K  V
.fi

.PP
With the
.B \-3
option, the sequence is printed in groups of 3 and only the frame-0
translation is shown, in three-letter amino acid code. The
.B \-3
option sets and requires
.BR "\-g 3" .

.PP
With the
.B \-t
option, coordinates are printed on top of each line of sequence
(at the end of each group) instead of at the left and right.
Because the coordinate labels mark the end of each group,
.B \-t
requires a nonzero
.B \-g
group size.

.nf
        10         20         30         40         50         60
ATTATTATCC ATTACACGAA GATTTAGTAT CATCTTTTTC TTAACTCTCC ACTTGCAAAG
TAATAATAGG TAATGTGCTT CTAAATCATA GTAGAAAAAG AATTGAGAGG TGAACGTTTC
.fi


.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.B \-h
Print brief help; includes version number and summary of all options.

.TP
.B \-3
Print the sequence in groups of 3, and show the frame-0 translation
in three-letter amino acid code. Sets and requires
.B \-g
to be 3. Incompatible with
.BR \-a .

.TP
.B \-a
Show the translation in all three top-strand reading frames, in
single-letter amino acid code, aligned with their codons. Sets and requires
.B \-g
to be 0 (no grouping). Incompatible with
.BR \-3 .

.TP
.BI \-f " <n>"
Number the first residue as
.I <n>
instead of 1.
.I <n> must be >= 1.
Useful for printing a region from the middle of a
larger sequence with its native coordinates.

.TP
.BI \-g " <n>"
Print the sequence in groups of
.I <n>
symbols, separated by single spaces. The default is 10. A value of 0
means no grouping (a continuous run of symbols).
.I <n>
must be >= 0.

.TP
.BI \-n " <n>"
Print
.I <n>
symbols per line. The default is 60. This must be an exact multiple
of the group size.
.I <n>
must be >= 10.

.TP
.B \-s
Print only the top (single) strand. By default, both top and bottom
(complement) strands are printed.

.TP
.B \-t
Print coordinates above each line of sequence, at the end of each
group, instead of at the left and right. Requires a nonzero
.B \-g
group size.

.TP
.BI \-\-informat " <s>"
Assert that the input
.I seqfile
is in format
.IR <s> ,
bypassing format autodetection. Valid choices for
.I <s>
include
.BR fasta ,
.BR embl ,
.BR genbank ,
.BR ddbj ,
.BR uniprot ,
and the aligned formats
.BR stockholm ,
.BR a2m ,
.BR a3m ,
.BR afa ,
.BR clustal ,
.BR phylip ,
.BR psiblast ,
and
.BR selex .

.TP
.B \-\-dna
Assert that
.I seqfile
contains DNA sequence. By default, the alphabet is autodetected from
the first sequence. Incompatible with
.BR \-\-rna .

.TP
.B \-\-rna
Assert that
.I seqfile
contains RNA sequence. By default, the alphabet is autodetected from
the first sequence. Incompatible with
.BR \-\-dna .



